{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"3852f4e72a0598af","type":"group","x":-1120,"y":-400,"width":3481,"height":2080,"label":"Flow example scenario"},
		{"id":"2831ec64bdab7730","type":"group","x":787,"y":4020,"width":290,"height":820,"label":"Current flow"},
		{"id":"6a9237f16dd40c6c","type":"text","text":"## Step 3: Mapping Fields \n\n* Where does this source field go in the MDM model?\n* Map the source field to target field\n\t* source fields are the fields which are derived from the source system.\n\t* target fields are the fields which are predefined in the MDM hub.\n* It is used for converting heterogeneous source data into single, standardized MDM structure that can be compared, organized, governed and merged.  \n* Which source field populates which MDM field?","x":740,"y":610,"width":680,"height":267},
		{"id":"759713542d2f267d","type":"text","text":"A company has **three systems** managing customer data:\n\n1. **CRM System** – Sales team\n    \n2. **ERP System** – Finance & billing\n    \n3. **Support System** – Customer service\n\n\nEach system stores the **same real-world customer differently**.","x":256,"y":-60,"width":567,"height":220},
		{"id":"9ed9c30a88210b2e","type":"text","text":"`Source system` -> `mapping` -> `base objects` -> `matching` -> `merge` -> `golden record`\n","x":300,"y":-320,"width":480,"height":80},
		{"id":"f28b3ffa4a1ce93b","type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Source System Records (Raw Reality)\n\n**CRM Record:**\n\n```\ncustomer_id: C123\nname: Rahul Sharma\nemail: rahul.sharma@gmail.com\nphone: 9876543210\n```\n\n**ERP Record:**\n\n```\ncust_no: 45678\nfull_name: R. Sharma\nemail_address: rsharma@gmail.com\nbilling_address: Pune, MH\n```\n\n**Support Record:**\n\n```\nuser_id: U998\nname: Rahul S.\ncontact: 9876543210\ncity: Pune\n```\n\n","x":-860,"y":530,"width":660,"height":607},
		{"id":"22562de940492a0d","type":"text","text":"## Step 2 Base Entity Configuration\n\nEach source is stored as a base entity.\n\n|base_object_id|source_system|source_record_id|attribute|value|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|BO_001|CRM|C123|name|Rahul Sharma|\n|BO_001|CRM|C123|email|[rahul.sharma@gmail.com](mailto:rahul.sharma@gmail.com)|\n|BO_002|ERP|45678|full_name|R. Sharma|\n|BO_003|SUPPORT|U998|phone|9876543210|\n\n- **No transformation**\n    \n- **No deduplication**\n    \n- **Source fidelity preserved**","x":-70,"y":530,"width":740,"height":427},
		{"id":"6b62fa5c07605f17","type":"text","text":"## Step 4: Matching (Duplicate Detection)\n\nprocess of identifying which standardized base object represent the same real world entity.\n\n\n```example\nC-1:\n\tfirstname = Rahul\n\tphone = 123456789\n\tcity = pune\n\t\nC-2:\n\tfirstname = Rahul S\n\tphone = 123456789\n\tcity = pune\n\t\nHumans or by naked eyes we can say both the records are same\nBut system cannot decide both the records are same.\n```\n\n\nMatching rules:\n\n- Phone match → high confidence    \n- Name similarity → medium confidence\n- City match → low confidence\n\n#### Step 1: Select match attributes:\n\nMatching only considers **specific MDM fields**, for example:\n\n- phoneNumber\n- emailAddress\n- firstName + lastName\n- governmentId (if available)\n\n#### Step 2: Apply Comparison Logic\n\nEach attribute can use a different comparison type:\n\n|Attribute|Comparison Type|\n|---|---|\n|phoneNumber|Exact|\n|emailAddress|Exact|\n|name|Fuzzy|\n|address|Fuzzy|\n\n#### Step 3: Calculate Match Score\n\n#### Step 4: Classify the Match\n\n\n\n","x":1520,"y":353,"width":741,"height":1209},
		{"id":"eed373a60589914f","type":"text","text":"- Data is duplicated\n    \n- No system knows about the others\n    \n- Reports will be inconsistent","x":-709,"y":1280,"width":359,"height":120},
		{"id":"4886f6bb00338f7b","type":"text","text":"Source system","x":807,"y":4040,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1c2b6f7c2ce7bc9e","type":"text","text":"Data validation","x":807,"y":4160,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cc20044db8a50d76","type":"text","text":"base object","x":807,"y":4280,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b941216cb22ef42a","type":"text","text":"configuration","x":807,"y":4400,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"dfb4811d1e8a8bb7","type":"text","text":"mapping","x":807,"y":4520,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a255ac6dcf45cb2a","type":"text","text":"matching","x":807,"y":4640,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"73506041d5a719a1","type":"text","text":"merge","x":807,"y":4760,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d7291dac0f7f9f83","type":"text","text":"Incoming Record  \n   |  \n   v  \n────────────────────────  \n1️⃣ QUALITY VALIDATION  \n────────────────────────  \n• Phone format check  \n• Email format check  \n• Address presence check  \n• Date format check\n\n   |  \n   |-- ❌ FAIL →   \n   |              (Record blocked)  \n   |  \n   v  \n────────────────────────  \n2️⃣ ENRICHMENT  \n────────────────────────  \n• Address → Geocoding  \n• Location enrichment\n\n   |  \n   |-- ⚠ API failure → Apply fallback  \n   |  \n   v  \n────────────────────────  \n3️⃣ SAVE RECORD  \n────────────────────────  \n  \n• Ready for Matching","x":1490,"y":3995,"width":590,"height":845},
		{"id":"115753d7e780ebbe","type":"text","text":"### Questions:\n\n1. When the data validation should trigger?\n2. ","x":2260,"y":3540,"width":676,"height":289},
		{"id":"429d16dc2ef21049","type":"text","text":"Quality check starts","x":2435,"y":3920,"width":327,"height":120},
		{"id":"cf95baff898a1854","type":"text","text":"What is the process for data validation?\n\nhow should we read the data?\n- panda\n- spark\n\n* We need to set the rules for every fields so that we can check on data. \n* Run the validation script for trigger.\n* Store the expected result in the separate collection\n* make the separate api for getting those validation results.. \n","x":2366,"y":4400,"width":454,"height":340},
		{"id":"3f39b7c635507fa2","type":"text","text":"Need data for quality check\n(as of now data is being stored in mongodb)\nCheck the required fields are present in data.","x":2435,"y":4160,"width":327,"height":160},
		{"id":"bdcf740b282d161e","x":3220,"y":3540,"width":440,"height":400,"type":"text","text":""}
